  <body>
    <h1>Support</h1>

    <p>
      This page is for WoW Forever Talents, the iOS and iPadOS app that goes with the
      website wowforever.be.
    </p>

    <h2>Getting in touch</h2>
    <p>
      Questions, problems and requests can go to <strong>contact@wowforever.be</strong>.
      Every message is read. Please say which iPhone or iPad you use, which version of
      iOS it runs, and what you were doing when something went wrong.
    </p>

    <h2>Things people ask</h2>

    <p><strong>The app is free and there is nothing to buy.</strong> There is no account
      and no login. Nothing in the app is locked.</p>

    <p><strong>The talent calculator does not match my game.</strong> World of Warcraft:
      Forever is still in beta, and Blizzard changes talents during a beta. The app says
      which build of the game its data comes from. When the game changes, an app update
      follows.</p>

    <p><strong>A shared build link does not open.</strong> A build lives inside the link,
      so the whole link has to be copied, including everything after the question mark.
      The same link also opens in a browser on wowforever.be.</p>

    <p><strong>I get no notifications.</strong> Notifications are off until you allow
      them. Check Settings, Notifications, WoW Forever on your device. Turning them off
      again stops them; nothing else in the app depends on them.</p>

    <p><strong>The news does not refresh.</strong> The app keeps a copy of the news so it
      opens without a connection. Pull down on the list to fetch again.</p>

    <p><strong>The names of talents are in English in every language.</strong> That is on
      purpose. World of Warcraft has no translated Classic client, and a name that does
      not match what you see in the game helps nobody. The rest of the app is translated.</p>

    <h2>Privacy</h2>
    <p>
      What the app stores, and what it does not, is at
      <a href="https://wowforever.be/privacy/">wowforever.be/privacy</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>Not affiliated with Blizzard</h2>
    <p>
      This is an unofficial fan app. It is not affiliated with, endorsed by or sponsored
      by Blizzard Entertainment, Inc. World of Warcraft and Blizzard Entertainment are
      trademarks or registered trademarks of Blizzard Entertainment, Inc.
    </p>
  </body>
